id: flooded
name: Flooded
kind: conditions
# One stack per clock, so the Square stays Bog until the last attacker's clock runs out
# rather than the first. The cap only has to be out of anybody's reach, as Ignited's does.
maxStacks: 99
# Not a Combat Condition: the entry turns a Square into an Environment and never names one.
combatCondition: no
# The Battle Environment this mark turns the Square into while it is held. Read by
# `environmentIdOf`, which names no Environment.
becomes: bog-environment
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Water churns the ground to mud under you. You are in the Bog Environment.
text: >
  Flooded: the Elemental (Water) Profile's mark. "Any Squares occupied by Character(s) who
  take Damage from this Attacking Maneuver become the Bog Environment (see — Battle
  Environments) until the start of your next turn."

---

# --- The name is this system's ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Ignited's shape, turning an Environment rather than adding a Quality. There are no
# Squares, the Environment is picked on the character, so the Bog lands on whoever took the
# Damage, as a mark on the attacker's clock.
#
# The pick is never written to. `environmentIdOf` answers with what this mark `becomes`
# while it is held, and with the pick again once it runs out - which is what they were
# standing on the whole time. The tab keeps the picker on the pick and says "Now: Bog
# Environment" underneath.
#
# Every reader of the Environment asks `environmentIdOf`, so Bog is Bog everywhere: its
# effects, its Hardness range for a Ground Collision, and the breath - Underwater turned to
# Bog is somewhere they can breathe, and turning back is entering the water again.
#
# No effects of its own. What a bog does is the Bog Environment's file.
